<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mandonius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 205 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mandonius was a chief of the Ilergetes, an Iberian people of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, who led them with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indibilis">Indibilis</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. The brothers first served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and then joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-africanus">Scipio Africanus</a> in 209 BCE. They later rose against Roman rule, and after their defeat in 205 BCE, in which Indibilis fell, Mandonius was handed over to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> by his own people and executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mandonius.jpg" alt="Mandonius" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lleida-6-1_indibil_i_mandoni.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
